# A3 step 3 T02-GROUP (AiPlayerbot.Supervisor.Arbiter = 2 and AiPlayerbot.BotGroups.Manager.Types > 0, both default 0; design
# ws-00/projekt-durchleuchtung/A3-S3-T02-ENTWURF.md v0.4.3 section 7, build spec A3-S3-T02GROUP-BAUSPEC.md): the bot side of the
# group manager, SupervisorGroup.cpp. At the defaults nothing runs. This contract pins, each with a negative probe at the end:
#   (1)  the three manager calls (PostDirectiveAck, PostDirectiveLeft, group_mgr::IsManaged) once each in SupervisorGroup.cpp and
#        nowhere else on the bot side;
#   (2)  LeaveGroupMode defined once, never called from ~Supervisor (the logout thread may run it);
#   (3)  HandleMail only at the end of TakeMail, writing nothing;
#   (4)  RegisterMail called only in GroupTick, UnregisterMail only in ~Supervisor (two arguments, token compared);
#   (5)  the snapshot: PlayerTravelInfo::groupGoalQuest filled from GroupGoalSnapshot only (no GetSupervisor in TravelMgr.cpp);
#   (6)  R-c: an open quest target other than c is closed (group_goal), a PREPARE is cancelled (group_prepare);
#   (7)  PeekOwner never assigns the owner;
#   (8)  RESCUE: GroupTick starts with the rescueByGroup_ reset, returns early only without Group/Rescue mode and work, and
#        leaves RESCUE for the quest mode only behind rescueByGroup_;
#   (9)  GroupRelease leaves the group mode only behind the held-group check;
#   (10) the close loop lines (goal_close, prep_cancel with writer=) and the writer note (NoteWriter);
#   (11) Q4: one GroupHandlerOn definition, exactly two calls, a body that is either true or the cohort rule;
#   (12) following: MakeFollower once (after SameMapObject and FollowerIntact), MakeTurnIn once, no strategy string, the role
#        set only in StartFollow / UndoFollow, UndoFollow from LeaveGroupMode and the done teardown, StartFollow only from
#        ApplyMove and ApplyMove only from EnterGroup, ChangeGroup (Update, T33) and RESCUE -> GROUP (recheck 4);
#   (13) the T33 traps (Q8): Verb::Update stays the one VerbName case, VerbClass exists, the six reserved T33-1 names appear
#        nowhere;
#   (14) no teleport and no hop call, no number literal as ack state or reason;
#   (15) the FollowerSet list text only in QuestGroupWorld.cpp, whose header declares the six moved functions;
#   (16) GroupCopyFree once in ChooseTravelTargetAction.cpp, BandHeldByGroup twice in QuestBand.cpp;
#   (17) GateOffThread reads no supervisor, applies the cohort and counts only a live target;
#   (18) the [ArbiterGrp] formatter (sha) and the appended mailbox fields (the mailbox line tag itself stays once under PB/);
#   (19) the one SetOwner(Lane::Group, call sits in AdoptGroupOwner.
# Every check_* returns "" when it holds, else the reason; the negative probes reuse them on mutated text.
